From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] opengles: 3dtexture alpha applied once

The texture shaders multiply the color by its alpha (premultiplied output), so
blending has to take the source as is (GL_ONE). The 3D draw set blend_opt,
which blends with GL_SRC_ALPHA and multiplies by alpha a second time: the half
transparent edges of a texture with rounded corners came out darker than both
the texture and what is under it, a dark outline on a light background.
---
--- a/src/draw/opengles/lv_draw_opengles.c
+++ b/src/draw/opengles/lv_draw_opengles.c
@@ -917,7 +917,7 @@
     params.h_flip = dsc->h_flip;
     params.v_flip = dsc->v_flip;
     params.rb_swap = dsc->rb_swap;
-    params.blend_opt = true;
+    params.blend_opt = false;
     lv_opengles_render(&params);
 
     if(target_texture) {
